  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="dba52e8d-9daf-5ea4-a92f-5fdc5fdada3d" activityNameId="fe3916d7-1ab3-50b6-a431-44c5ec1ec8ef" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Smartphone, mid-tier, average phone, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Smartphone, mid-tier, average phone, at plant
The data set represents the production of smartphone with defined technical specifications; UUID: b1d39f62-703a-3104-9cc9-71baf50a9d6c
This dataset focuses on the average hi-tech smartphones with 4 - 6.5 inch screen size. The weight of the smartphone is defined to be about 160 grams. The data for average smartphones are mainly taken from the JRC technical report and other published articles. The modeled smartphone has a flash storage capacity of 32 GB and RAM capacity of 2 GB. According to the industry technology for IC smartphones, up to 6 stacked dies can be integrated in a single package to optimize density and performance. In the modeling, the area of wafer/die is assumed to be ~5.5 cm2 to represent total wafer logic area according to the literature.
Location: Data for global average for smartphone
Technology: The smartphone has a processing unit, flash storage, RAM, and other connectivity features for standard smartphones.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Literature &amp; own estimations
Extrapolations: Average technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_b1d39f62-703a-3104-9cc9-71baf50a9d6c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
